  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening comprehensive Primary Healthcare through Integrated  and Locally Driven Digital Health Solutions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Local Initiative For Digital Health (LIDH) is an initiative designed to accelerate the creation of a resilient, locally driven, interoperable, and people-centric digital health ecosystem in Maharashtra. Built upon Indias established digital public infrastructure, LIDH will provide a structured, consultative process to help national and state governments design, integrate, and scale digital health systems aligned with the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM) architecture.UNDP will provide high-level technical oversight and support, and strategic coordination for delivering four key outputs: improved availability and efficiency of primary healthcare services; a citizen-centric, inclusive, interoperable digital health ecosystem with end-to-end health records; strengthened stakeholder capacities for digitalization; and targeted BCC and IEC campaigns. The model is designed to be replicable and scalable for global reference through the WHO Global Initiative on Digital Health (GIDH) Transformation Toolbox.</narrative>
  </description>
